ntries has a significant domain shift  there's a lot of features which you  might not have in different countries  which might  you know consider different inputs and  also  uh the survival rate is generally lower  which can be due to  a reporting bias so for example uh  american hospitals are forced to report  uh deaths or any negative events  whereas hospitals and other countries  might not have to so this could bias the  output  but also it could simply be to overall  higher survival in countries such as for  example canada  and uh i should mention as a final note  that  we are working on improving this model  continuously  ideas that we worked on after this idea  were mostly  around improving the time prediction  which is of course very important for  the aforementioned  model we we got a workshop paper  at icml uh discussing  the idea of applying this with an earth  mover's distance  where the muscle stand distance between  your survival distribution over time and  ground truth survival distribution  is computed that gained a large  improvement over  time prediction and we're also  considering what happens in a more  realistic case where for example remodel  is trained  but you have data coming in regularly in  the form of simply hospitals  every day adding more patients and more  data how do you improve your model in a  way that  does not disrupt past performance  and uh so i'm i'm done thank you  okay and so i'll be talking about the  second point of information  that our tool will provide now and so  this was work that was done  by uh jean el veler a master student  under the supervision of andrea ludi at  the corporal technique  and so the problem here is to say so we  have an offer at  time t 0 and we want to estimate the  time to the next offer and the  quality of that next offer and so what  uh  jeannette did is that he used  data real real life data from cosmon  quebec 2012 to 2017  and he uh built a model  with poisson distribution where what he  did i